      "sha256": "029feb3185f43a1ed77c0fa9e250c50e82758c78b7544f8905782c2dda9eb9b6",
      "bytes": 2989,
      "line_count": 24,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "Extend python-dateutil's rrule module with RFC 5545 timezone interoperability. RDATE gains TZID/VALUE parameter support. rrule and rruleset gain timezone-aware __str__, equality/hash/repr, property accessors, iCalendar serialization, and set operations. rrulestr gains VCALENDAR auto-detection with V"
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "- RDATE supports TZID, VALUE=DATE, and VALUE=DATE-TIME parameters (same as EXDATE and DTSTART)."
        },
        {
          "line": 4,
          "text": "- rrulestr accepts an optional tzids parameter for TZID resolution: a mapping (name -> tzinfo), a callable (name -> tzinfo), or None (defaults to dateutil.tz.gettz)."
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "- rrule.__str__() emits DTSTART with a TZID parameter for non-UTC timezones, or a Z suffix for UTC. UNTIL follows the same pattern. rrulestr(str(rule)) round-trips correctly, including auto-generated timezone-aware dtstart values."
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "- rruleset.__str__() outputs DTSTART (from the first rrule), then RRULE, RDATE, EXRULE, EXDATE in order. Timezone-aware RDATE/EXDATE include TZID; UTC uses Z. EXRULE lines use the EXRULE: prefix."
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "- rrule.__eq__ compares all recurrence parameters. __hash__ is consistent with equality."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "- rrule.__repr__ produces a reconstructable expression using symbolic frequency names (YEARLY, WEEKLY, etc.). eval(repr(r)) yields an equivalent rrule."
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "- Read-only properties rrule.dtstart, rrule.freq, rrule.interval, rrule.until expose recurrence parameters."
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "- rrule.count() returns the count parameter directly when set, otherwise iterates (inherited from rrulebase)."
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "- rrule.to_ical() serializes as VCALENDAR/VEVENT. Non-UTC timezone-aware dtstart includes a VTIMEZONE with STANDARD component; TZOFFSETTO/TZOFFSETFROM derived from the UTC offset at dtstart."
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": "- rruleset.rrules, .rdates, .exrules, .exdates are read-only tuples in insertion order."
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "- rruleset.__eq__ compares all four component groups (dates sorted for order-independence)."
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "- rruleset.__repr__ produces a multi-line expression: rruleset() followed by .rrule(), .rdate(), .exrule(), .exdate() calls."
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "- rruleset.copy() creates a shallow copy with identical components."
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "- rruleset.union(other) combines all components from both sets. Raises TypeError for non-rruleset."
        },
        {
          "line": 17,
          "text": "- rruleset.subtract(other) adds other's rrules as exrules and rdates as exdates. Raises TypeError for non-rruleset."
        },
        {
          "line": 18,
          "text": "- rruleset.to_ical() serializes as VCALENDAR, emitting a VTIMEZONE block per unique non-UTC timezone."
        },
        {
          "line": 19,
          "text": "- rruleset.from_str(s) is a classmethod wrapping rrulestr with forceset=True."
        },
        {
          "line": 20,
          "text": "- rrulestr auto-detects BEGIN:VCALENDAR, extracts VTIMEZONE and VEVENT. Only recurrence properties (DTSTART, RRULE, RDATE, EXRULE, EXDATE) from the first VEVENT. RFC 5545 line unfolding is handled. Inline VTIMEZONE definitions take priority over tzids lookups."
        },
        {
          "line": 21,
          "text": "- A comment references \"RFC 5445\" instead of \"RFC 5545\"."
        },
        {
          "line": 22,
          "text": "- The error for conflicting timezones (TZID + Z suffix on same value) becomes \"date property specifies multiple timezones\"."
        },
        {
          "line": 24,
          "text": "IMPORTANT: Please work on this in a new branch from main and commit everything when you are done."
        }
      ]
    },
